menu "Fall startup calibration"
        config FALL_CALIB_MS
            int "Static calibration window at boot (ms, 0 = skip)"
            default 2000
            help
                The device must be perfectly still for this long after reset: the
                gyroscope zero-rate bias and the accelerometer magnitude scale are
                estimated from the window, then applied to every sample. Without it the
                gyro offset integrates into yaw (-2 deg/s was measured on this bench unit)
                and a |a| error biases the quiet/energy features. A window that moved is
                rejected rather than applied silently.

        config FALL_CALIB_TRIES
            int "Calibration attempts before giving up"
            default 5
            help
                Each attempt is FALL_CALIB_MS long. A window that moved is rejected and
                another is tried, so the operator does not have to reset at exactly the
                right moment. With 5 x 2000 ms the boot waits at most 10 s.

endmenu
